react
--react is js libary used to build single page applications

react features
1)virtual dom-It is a copy of real dom
             -It will compare and render the changes only using 
             diffing alogorithm and the entire process is called reconcialation
2)components architrecture  -navbar,footer,card,sidebar,jsx
3)single page application-it contains only one index.html

components--It is the piece of code which renders part of ui
1)functional components----Hooks(it is simply like built in functions)

1st component:
function Navbar(){
    return (<h1>navbar</h1)
}
export default Navbar

2nd component:
import Navbar from '/Navbar'

2)class components ---old---life cycle methods

props--properties
-----------------
--It is a object that is used to pass the information from parent to child

--react  will not rerender when the variable changes
--react re renders only when state changes 

State 
====
--It is like a variable it is used to handle the dynamic nature of 
a component or store the data

Hooks
====
--hooks are built in functions that is used to handle react features

1)useState
===========
--It is a hook that is used to manage the state

import{useState} from 'react'

let[state,setSate]=useState(0);

{count}
<button onClick={()=>setCount(count+1)}>inc</button>

Theory
--state--It is like a variable name
--state=1
setSate - it is a function that is used to change the value 
         of a state